berkeley-master.logic.r1: argue/equivocates: A1: "unconceived" is taken as conceiving the objects while they are at that very moment unconceived, which one's own act of conceiving contradicts in A1 C1 and as conceiving, as the content of one's thought, that the objects exist with no one conceiving them where conceive_unconceived is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C (S4) does not follow (berkeley-master.logic.r1.sense1)
berkeley-master.logic.r1: argue/countermodel: C (S4): conceive_mind_indep = T, conceive_unconceived = T, conceive_unconceived_2 = F
